IDENTITIES
===========================

Every distinct name and email pair in the extracted history, most active first.
Commits counts distinct commits; the role counts show how often the identity
appeared as author or committer.

Alice Dev <alice@example.com>
  Commits:      2 total (1 as author, 2 as committer)
  First seen:   2023-01-01T09:00:00+01:00
  Last seen:    2023-02-01T09:00:00+01:00
Carol <7+carol@users.noreply.github.com>
  Commits:      1 total (1 as author, 0 as committer)
  First seen:   2023-03-01T09:00:00+01:00
  Last seen:    2023-03-01T09:00:00+01:00
Carol <7+mallory@users.noreply.github.com>
  Commits:      1 total (0 as author, 1 as committer)
  First seen:   2023-03-01T09:00:00+01:00
  Last seen:    2023-03-01T09:00:00+01:00
Bob Ops <alice@example.com>
  Commits:      1 total (1 as author, 0 as committer)
  First seen:   2023-02-01T09:00:00+01:00
  Last seen:    2023-02-01T09:00:00+01:00

COLLISIONS
----------
One email under several names, or one name under several emails, is invisible
commit by commit. It is how both impersonation and a misconfigured client look.

Emails used under more than one name:
  alice@example.com used by: Alice Dev, Bob Ops

Names used with more than one email:
  Carol used by: 7+carol@users.noreply.github.com, 7+mallory@users.noreply.github.com

PLACEHOLDER IDENTITIES
----------------------
Identities naming no real mailbox: a reserved or machine-local domain, or an
empty field. That is what an unconfigured client or a deliberately anonymous
commit looks like. Each commit using one is flagged in its COMMIT_INFO.txt.

  Alice Dev <alice@example.com>: placeholder domain example.com
  Bob Ops <alice@example.com>: placeholder domain example.com

GITHUB NOREPLY CONFLICTS
------------------------
A noreply address <id>+<handle>@users.noreply.github.com names an account by
its permanent ID. One ID under several handles is what a rename produces, and
also a forged address; one handle under several IDs is not something a rename
produces.

  account ID 7 appears with handles: carol, mallory
